  "notes": "A common word for fainting or losing consciousness. Used in both everyday conversation and dramatic contexts (novels, manga, etc.).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {気絶|きぜつ}する: to faint, to pass out\n- {気絶|きぜつ}しそうになる: to nearly faint\n- {気絶|きぜつ}から{覚|さ}める: to regain consciousness\n- {一瞬|いっしゅん}{気絶|きぜつ}する: to black out for a moment\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {失神|しっしん}: fainting — more medical/formal\n- {意識|いしき}を{失|うしな}う: to lose consciousness — clinical description\n- {卒倒|そっとう}: collapsing — emphasizes the physical falling",
